WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.640
I don't want to get into the politics
of gun ownership.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.400
I'm British, I'm not exactly qualified,
but I will say that Switzerland has

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.800
a very high rate of people who own guns,
and a pretty low rate of people

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.360
who are hurt by guns. 

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.240
This is the Brünnlisau shooting range,
about two hours from Zürich.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.000
And I think it's the best possible
demonstration of the attitude

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.720
that Switzerland has to both firearms
and firearms safety.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.280
You fire your rifle from there. 

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.600
The targets are over there. 

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.000
And in between them is a major highway.
And it's safe.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.337
IN SWISS GERMAN:

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.520
Rifle shooting is
a national sport in Switzerland.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.600
Service in the military
is compulsory for men, albeit

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.280
these days with the choice to take on
civilian public service work instead.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.040
For those who do choose military service,
a lot of them decide

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.040
to keep their firearm when they finish,
which means that yes,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.440
there are a lot of people
with guns in Switzerland,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.880
but they pretty much all have
thorough training in how to use them.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.040
All right. So I lie down... 

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.760
- Yes, yes.
- All the way down. OK.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.160
- OK. Your target is number seven. 

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.520
Number seven... I thought
 this was a magnifier.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.000
It's not a magnifier. 

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.360
You just have to be very accurate. 

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.200
Without munition.
- Without. Yes.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.600
- You look at the target and push.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:24.960
[hammer clicks]

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.760
- I think I'd have missed there. But...
- Yeah?

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.520
- OK. All right. Let's try it for real.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.760
If you're shooting a rifle here, you're
lying down and you cannot see the road.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.080
Anything you fire
that's traveling fast enough 

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.440
to go over that wall
just can't hit the road.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.720
That just isn't a possible trajectory
for a bullet that can damage anything

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.400
other than the hill
and, of course, the targets.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.480
That goes up against my shoulder, here.
- In the position, yes.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.360
- And gets held with this hand here.
- Mmhm.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.280
- And I just have to line up...

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.400
- Look to the target and... push.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.520
- Missed. Gah, I swore the recoil was
going to hit me in the eye there.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.120
Closer!

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.040
High and right. Okay!

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.560
five. I'm going the other way now. 

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.560
- Hey!
- Hey, that's a ten!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.000
This is a ten, yes!

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.080
Got there in the end. 

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.200
Nine. It's good.
- I'll take that.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.800
That's, what, 56 out of 100,
and I got one in the bullseye.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.960
- Yes.
- I'll take that. 

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:09.000
Thank you very much. 

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.720
Danke schön.
- You're welcome.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.480
- Now, there is the reasonable question:
well, what if someone were to stand up?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.240
Then they could see and hit the road. 

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.840
Well, again: training,
it's unlikely to happen.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.960
And also, breaking the safety rules

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.720
when you're surrounded by military-trained
firearm enthusiasts is... 

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:25.920
not a great plan?

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.160
"What if you stand up"
is basically the same question as

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.120
"what if you decide to point
the rifle at someone"? 

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.320
You will very rapidly
not be holding a rifle anymore.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.680
If someone wants to cause harm with a gun,
 this is not the way they'd do it.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.800
Joining a rifle club, getting all
the permits and then deciding

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.240
to throw all that away
to take a potshot at a car just once?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.320
I'm not sure there's anyone who's sensible
enough to do the first bits of that,

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.800
and unhinged enough to do the last part.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.920
And if there is,
they've never made it here.

